4. business-pay `pay_filer` takes the payment event. These cases are acknowledged without action:
   - an empty or unparseable body;
   - a payment that is not COMPLETED;
   - corp types MHR and BTR;
   - a BC payment with no filing identifier;
   - a filing already carrying a payment completion date.

   A bad JWT gets 403. An unknown filing gets 404, so the message is retried. Otherwise the filing is saved PAID. continuationIn filings go to AWAITING_REVIEW and never reach the filer. The others are published to the filer, then to the emailer. Publish errors are swallowed after the commit, so a lost message is not resent. entity-pay is the older NATS version of this step. pay-api, outside this area, sends the payment event.
